      "segment_id": "S00001",
      "start_char": 0,
      "end_char": 195,
      "text": "MEXICO\n44. Alongside weak per capita income\n3000 50\ngrowth, poverty rates in Mexico have\nremained stubbornly high. Poverty rates have 2900\nconsistently hovered around 40 percent but rose 2800 45\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00002",
      "start_char": 195,
      "end_char": 412,
      "text": "in 2020 due to the pandemic. With the economic 2700\nrecovery, real income has rebounded, and\n2600 40\npoverty rates have fallen back to pre-pandemic\n2500\nlevels.11\n2400 35\n45. There are persistent, stark regional 2300\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00003",
      "start_char": 412,
      "end_char": 617,
      "text": "inequalities that show no sign of narrowing. 2200 30\nBoth the Northern and Central regions of Mexico\n2100\nhave greatly benefitted from proximity to the\n2000 25\nU.S. Meanwhile, the South of the country has\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00004",
      "start_char": 617,
      "end_char": 799,
      "text": "suffered from little integration with the rest of\nthe country and the U.S., and limited economic\nopportunity. This has resulted in low levels of\ninvestment in health, education, and\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00005",
      "start_char": 799,
      "end_char": 1027,
      "text": "infrastructure, thereby reinforcing a significantly poorer economic performance and lower real\nincomes.\n11 Given public health restrictions, income surveys were not conducted in 2020Q2 resulting in missing data for this\nperiod.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00006",
      "start_char": 1027,
      "end_char": 1228,
      "text": "INTERNATIONAL MONETARY FUND 23\n$XEM\nlaeR\nnoitalupoP\nfo\ntnecreP\nTrends in Labor Income and Poverty\nReal Per Capita Labor Income 1/\nPercent of Population in Labor Income Poverty 2/ (RHS)\nSource: CONEVAL\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00007",
      "start_char": 1228,
      "end_char": 1402,
      "text": "1/Real per capita labor income is taken from CONEVAL's Cuadro de Indicadores ITLP\nstatisticalreleaseand defined as per capital labor income (including informal labor income)\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00008",
      "start_char": 1402,
      "end_char": 1624,
      "text": "deflated by CPI. Data on per capita labor income is missing for 2020Q2 due the impact of\nthe COVID-19 pandemic on data collection.\n2/ The official labor income poverty line is determined by CONEVAL using its labor poverty\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00009",
      "start_char": 1624,
      "end_char": 1856,
      "text": "index methodology.\n4000\n3500\n3000\n2500\n2000\n1500\n$XEM\nlaeR\nLabor Income by Region 1/\n125\nNorthern Mexico 2/\nCentral Mexico 2/ 120\nSouthern Mexico 2/\n115\n110\n105\n100\n95\n90\n85\n80\n001\n=\n1Q0102\nxednI\nTrends in Labor Income by Region 1/\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00010",
      "start_char": 1856,
      "end_char": 2094,
      "text": "Northern Mexico 2/\nCentral Mexico 2/\nSouthern Mexico 2/\nSources: CONEVAL, INEGI;andIMFstaff calculations\n1/Real per capita labor income is taken from CONEVAL's Cuadro de Indicadores ITLP statisticalreleaseand defined as per capital labor "
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00011",
      "start_char": 2094,
      "end_char": 2257,
      "text": "income (including\ninformal labor income) deflated by CPI. Data on per capita labor income is missing for 2020Q2 due to the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on data\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00012",
      "start_char": 2257,
      "end_char": 2412,
      "text": "collection. Regional averages are calculated as the average of state-level per capita income from CONEVAL weighted by the share of the economically active\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00013",
      "start_char": 2412,
      "end_char": 2589,
      "text": "population aged 15+ that the state contributes to the broad geographic region. This data is taken from INEGI's National Survey of Occupation and\nEmployment statistical release.\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00014",
      "start_char": 2589,
      "end_char": 2741,
      "text": "2/ Northern Mexico includes the states of Aguascalientes, Baja California, Baja California Sur, Coahuila de Zaragoza, Chihuahua,Durango, Nayarit, Nuevo\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00015",
      "start_char": 2741,
      "end_char": 2894,
      "text": "León, San Luis Potosí, Sinaloa, Sonora, Tamaulipas, and Zacatecas. Central Mexico includes the states of Colima, Ciudad de México, Guanajuato, Guerrero,\n"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "S00016",
      "start_char": 2894,
      "end_char": 3115,
      "text": "Hidalgo, Jalisco, México, Michoacán de Ocampo, Morelos, Puebla, Querétaro, Tlaxcala, and Veracruz de Ignacio de la Llave. Southern Mexicoincludes the\nstates ofCampeche, Chiapas, Oaxaca, Quintana Roo, Tabasco, and Yucatán."
